tasks
    T62
        title       Package layout and import rules
        status      done
        priority    high
        description
            Fix the package's folders and what may import what, enforced by lint, before the tooling is built.
        acceptance
            - Lint encodes the package's top folders and what may import what between them: the core (everything in
              `src/` outside `src/host/`), the host, `fixtures/`, `tests/` and `bench/`. It does not encode the shape
              inside a folder. This Task moves no file: each folder is created by the Task that fills it (@task.V3.T63
              the test tooling and the first fixture folder, @task.V3.T64 `tests/rules/`, @task.V3.T66 `bench/`,
              @task.V3.T67 the other fixture folders, @task.V3.T68 `tests/types/`).
            - Lint refuses, for `.ts` and `.tsx` files: anything in `src/` outside `src/host/`, except `src/index.ts`,
              importing from `src/host/`; `src/` importing a fixture, test or bench; a fixture importing from `src/`
              anything but `src/index.ts` and `src/host/testing/index.ts`; a test or bench importing from `src/`
              anything but those two, `src/host/inspect.ts` and `src/host/trace.ts`.
            - Each rule has a planted violation it refuses and a permitted import it allows.
            - `nub run check`, `nub run lint:rules` and `vp test` pass.
    T63
        title       A Story drives the real Runtime over fakes
        status      done
        priority    high
        blocked_by  [@T62]
        description
            Build `Story`, `Fake` and the run in `src/host/testing/`, with a runtime cut in `src/host/inspect.ts`,
            proven on a transfers fixture and one Pay Story.
        acceptance
            - `Story.app(setup, { id, fixtures, world })` takes the app's real `runtimeSetup`, chains steps (ensure,
              detach, send, world, advance, reload, checkpoint, `dispose(ref, { how })` with `how: "forget"` for forget,
              disposeRuntime), and is inert data until `run()`, the only boundary. Every chained Story exposes its
              `Story.Step` array, and a run accepts a step array, which the reload sweep and generated Stories use.
              Checkpoint names are typed: reading an unknown one is a type error.
            - Fixtures cover every service the app's contracts list; a missing one is a type error (no `Layer<any>`).
            - `Fake.server(name, { truth, initial, endpoints, controls })` holds run-scoped, Schema'd truth that lasts
              across reloads; `Fake.call` endpoints return `{ truth, exit }` typed by their Schemas, `Fake.control`
              changes truth, and `Fake.Lost` reaches the port's own error through the port fake, a plain `Layer.effect`
              of the app's service. Wire words live on the endpoint: `hold({ at })`, `release` and `drop({ at })`. There
              is no `answer` word and no cast. The fake store has `hold`, `refuse` and `release` (`Fake.storage`).
            - A checkpoint holds the time, `inspect(runtime)` (the public runtime cut, @plan.Inspection.O1), what each
              fake received and its truth, and the store; tests read them only through the Plan's reads: `read(ref)`,
              `read(server)` (truth), `read(endpoint)` (the calls it received, with status; @plan.Pending.D8),
              `records`, `inspection`, `now`, and `run.evidence` for endings.
            - A dead page's released call or write never completes its waiter: evidence, store records and `inspection`
              are equal before and after the release (the handler may run and truth change, @spec.Stories.R13).
              `disposeRuntime` runs the public Runtime's dispose.
            - Every step word and every wire and storage word has a test. A Story run twice gives equal evidence. A run
              arms no host timer. A dead page writes nothing after a reload.
            - The test tooling's Spec (@spec.Stories, skill:to-spec) states the shape above, from @plan.Testing and the
              reuse proposal, as its Requirements and Invariants; the tooling's tests cite it.
            - The transfers fixture is one folder (contracts, machine, server, stories) with Story tests; its stories
              include one long run of about 100 steps, which @task.V3.T66 times.
            - The tooling is the public `flow-state/testing` and `flow-state/inspect` design, not exported in P2
              (@task.V3.T29 exports testing, @task.V3.T49 inspect); Flow's tests reach it by its path in the package.
            - One Pay Story passes: a `confirm` whose response is never answered (held at response, never released),
              time past the commit's deadline, a reload; the payment reads unknown and the shop handled exactly
              one `confirm`.
            - `nub run faults` over the new tests: a dead core fails every one.
            - An idiomatic-Effect review by a second Opus agent, using `effect-api-documentation`, leaves no finding
              open without a reason.
            - `vp test`, `nub run check` and `nub run lint:rules` pass.

            1. Chain (@spec.Stories.R1, @spec.Stories.R2, @spec.Stories.R3, @spec.Stories.I1 to @spec.Stories.I3):
               `tests/stories/story.test.ts`: `Story.app(transfersSetup, { id, fixtures })` chains every step word; a
               fixture Layer counting builds is 0 after two branches from one prefix and 1 per page after `run()`; the
               prefix's `steps` are unchanged; `run({ steps: s.steps })` equals `s.run()`; `@ts-expect-error` on reading
               an unknown checkpoint, a duplicate and a widened name.
            2. Fixtures cover the contracts (R7, I19): `@ts-expect-error` on a Story with no fixture for `BankApi` and
               on two fixtures of it; `runtimeSetup` has no `Layer<any>` (grep) and a setup without its services Layer
               is a type error; the setup's own services Layer, counting builds, stays at 0 in a run.
            3. Fake server (R8 to R11, I8, I9, I12, I13): `tests/stories/fake.test.ts`: a `Bank.limit` control makes the
               next transfer Declined; `read(Bank)` shows truth after each; the bank contract over `Fake.world`, outside
               a Story; `@ts-expect-error` on an Exit of other types, an unknown endpoint or control, a wrong control
               input, an `answer` word; no cast in fixtures or tests (grep). `tests/stories/wire.test.ts`: hold at
               request then release runs the handler once at the release (truth changes then); hold at response runs it
               at once; drop at request leaves truth and ends unknown via the port's NoResponse; drop at response
               changes truth once and ends unknown; each status in `read(Bank.transfer)`.
               `tests/stories/storage.test.ts`: `Fake.storage.hold` keeps every call out until release (WriteAhead R13);
               `refuse` ends NotSent StorageRefused with no call; batches logged.
            4. Cut (R12, I15, I16): a checkpoint's `now`, `inspection` (lane `state` InFlight then none),
               `read(account)`, `read(Bank)`, `read(Bank.transfer)` and `records` equal values derived from the steps;
               reading twice is equal.
            5. Dead page (R13, I10, I14): `tests/stories/reload.test.ts`: a write held across a reload, then released,
               is aborted; a call held at request across a reload, then released, is handled once; either release leaves
               `run.evidence`, `records` and `inspection` equal to the checkpoint before it (planted fault: the release
               completes the waiter); `disposeRuntime` ends `inspection`'s lifecycle Disposed and a call on the wire
               unknown Disposed at 5 s (Actors I35).
            6. Every word, reproducible, timer-free, dead page silent (R3 to R6, R14, I4 to I7, I17, I18):
               `steps.test.ts` has one case per step word (ensure, detach, send, dispose, dispose forget,
               disposeRuntime, world, advance, reload, checkpoint); `fake.test.ts` script faults reject StoryFailed
               (release with nothing held, unused hold, drop, storage hold and refuse, a throwing handler, a fixture
               that fails to build, a send after disposeRuntime); every fixture Story run twice gives equal evidence,
               checkpoints and end with no host timer called; a settle that never ends rejects StoryTurnLimit Settle.
            7. Spec: @spec.Stories states this shape; every tooling test title cites its rule.
            8. Transfers folder: `fixtures/transfers/{contracts,machine,server,stories}.ts` with a `bank.contract.ts`;
               `long` has 90 to 110 steps and one idempotency key per transfer (WriteLanes I6).
            9. Not exported (R15): no public route re-exports `src/host/testing` or `inspect` (grep); tests reach them
               by path.
            10. Pay (Restore R3, I6): `tests/pay/pay.test.ts`: confirm held at response, never released, 61 s, reload:
                row uncertain and not pending, lane Held, endings unknown TimedOut then unknown Restored,
                `read(Shop.confirm)` one call held at response; still one 10 s later.
            11. Dead core: `nub run faults` fails every new test on the dead core; the tooling faults in
                `tests/faults.ts` are rewritten for the new code (dead-page answer, aborted write fails its waiter, step
                left unsettled).
            12. Idiomatic-Effect review by a second Opus agent; findings closed or reasoned.
            13. `vp test`, `nub run check`, `nub run lint:rules` at zero.

            Decision (agent): `inspect(runtime)` lanes keep `operation` (the definition's name, as addresses use it) and
            add `contract` and `state`; the Shape's `operation: "Bank/transfer"` is read as the contract id. Reverse:
            rename. Decision (agent): `Fake.call` takes `failure` always (`Schema.Never` for none), so no default needs
            a cast. Decision (agent): a server is an Effect of `FakeWorld` with each endpoint's words and each control's
            word as its properties; an endpoint named like an Effect member would shadow it (doc Gotcha). Reverse: a
            separate key. Decision (agent): Pay's setup is real: `fixtures/pay/shop-http.ts` is a minimal production
            adapter (200 or NoResponse) so its setup has a services Layer; a Story never builds it (story test). Outside
            the May change list. Decision (agent): static checks (types, not exported) sit inside tests that also read
            the core, so the dead core fails each; the bank contract test checks the fake alone and stays green on a
            dead core by design. Finding: the `refused-turn-reported` core fault is missed by the suite; it is not a
            tooling rule and predates this Task (no deleted test exercised a refused turn). Left for T64's run rules.
