    T70
        title       Generated Stories
        status      done
        priority    high
        blocked_by  [@T64, @T67]
        description
            Build `propertyTest` in `src/host/testing/`: it generates `Story.Step` arrays from a fixture's step samples,
            each `Fake.server`'s controls and the wire words on its open calls, runs them with `run({ steps })`, applies
            the run rules, shrinks a failure by removing steps and prints it as a chained `Story.app(...)` expression.
        acceptance
            - The same seed gives the same Stories.
            - A planted fault is found from a seed and shrunk to under ten steps, and the failure prints as a Story to
              paste into a fixture.
            - Nothing generated is stored, except each fixture's stress Story below, which is saved as ordinary
              fixture code.
            - It runs over every fixture in `tests/generated/`.
            - Two profiles, from the usual and stress sections of `fixture-catalogue`: usual (realistic think times, a
              healthy server, at most 5% domain failures) and stress (bursts, faults drawn on every call and storage
              write, reloads, an offline span); a test names its profile, as in `propertyTest(fixture, { profile:
              "stress" })`.
            - A pair sweep: for each fixture, every reachable pair of a write's lifecycle phase and a fault (reload, a
              lost answer, a refused storage write, disposal, and the rest of the catalogue's grid) is driven once with
              the usual profile until a write reaches that phase, then given that fault, with the run rules applied;
              unreachable pairs are counted and named. The pair sweep is the deterministic floor of the test gate;
              random stress seeds add breadth, with a fixed seed list in the gate and more outside it.
            - Every fixture has a stress Story: a stress run from a fixed seed, printed as a chained `Story.app(...)`
              and saved in the fixture, so the bench and the reload sweep use it like any hand-written Story.

            - R1 (acceptance 1): two `generate` runs of one fixture, profile and seed emit equal step arrays and equal
              printed text; a different seed emits different steps.
            - R2 (acceptance 2; false pass): in `tests/generated/`, (a) an edge fault (a port fake that re-sends a lost
              call under a fresh id) and (b) one named core fault of `tests/faults.ts`, planted, are each falsified from
              a fixed seed and shrunk to under ten printed steps (Arbitrary shrinks draws, so the count is of the
              printed Story); the printed text itself is evaluated and re-run, and breaks the same rule.
            - R3 (acceptance 3; a constraint, not a check): nothing generated is written to a file; the stress Stories
              are pasted by hand as fixture code.
            - R4 (acceptance 4): a test lists `fixtures/` and fails on a fixture with no samples.
            - R5 (acceptance 5; `fixture-catalogue` lines 1064-1097): usual draws think times 80 ms to 20 s, server
              latency 50 to 800 ms log-uniform with a 2% tail of 2 to 5 s, at most 5% domain failures, no fault, reload
              or disposal. Stress draws gaps of 0 to 20 ms, bursts, and per request an answer of Ok 35, Fail 10, Lost
              10, LostButLanded 10, FailButLanded 5, Never 5, slow (1 to 90 s) 10, reordered 10, late 5; per write batch
              ack 75, refuse 15, hang 5, land unheard 5; exactly one offline span of 5 to 120 s in which every answer is
              Lost or Never; per step reload 3%, Runtime disposal 1%, actor disposal or forget 1%. Each mix is asserted
              over generated runs.
            - R6 (acceptance 6): the pair sweep crosses 8 phases (Acknowledging, Unsent, Withdrawing, Recapturing,
              Resending, OnWire, Cancelling, Held) with 7 faults (reload, lost answer, storage refusal, actor disposal,
              forget, release, disposal bound): 56 cells per fixture. A cell is reached only when its fault fires while
              a write stands in its phase. The drive is `DRIVE`, the usual profile plus lost answers and storage holds
              and refusals (amendment, coordinator-accepted). Expected unreachable cells are named per fixture from its
              Specs' lifecycle rules, each with its reason, never from a recorded run.
            - R7 (acceptance 6): the gate runs the pair sweep and 10 usual and 20 stress seeds per fixture, split into
              slices across test files, never thinned; `FLOW_SEEDS` adds more outside it. Work still pending at the
              horizon is inconclusive, counted, and fails the test.
            - R8 (acceptance 7; T71): each fixture's `stories` holds a stress Story whose steps equal the print of its
              seed; the reload sweep and the bench pick it up. `strideOf` is dropped: every stress Story, T71's palette
              and number-input ones included, is swept at every step under a raised test timeout.
            - R9 (T71): the palette gives a disabled command no shortcut (`shortcutsOf`); its pages and queries are one
              frame stack; NUMBER-10 commits only on release, as upstream does (the coordinator's ruling).
            - G1 (T64): the sweep asserts a numeric skip bound per Story, derived from its hold-to-release windows; a
              dead core breaks it.
            - G2 (T64): each of the six narrow rules (WriteLanes I3, I6, I15; Turn I9, I14; Restore I1) is widened, with
              a rule test over a crafted run that the narrow rule passes.
            - G3 (T67): Turn I30 is a run rule, red on a crafted run that republishes an equal part as a new object.
            - G4 (T67): every fixture Story also runs under another session seed and shuffled load order, and ends with
              a reload with every writer attached, under the rules.
            - G5 (T67): Stories I7 states the bound as built (a crossing batch is rejected whole), with a test.
            - G6 (T67, T69): `nub run faults` counts over-1 MB output, a timeout or a missing summary as not caught, and
              plants into the whole package's tests, `src/` included.
        comment     2026-11-16T01:19:55Z
            Done 2026-11-16: `propertyTest`, the pair sweep and generated Stories; PASS at 554531f2 (offline span 5 to
            120 s virtual, bursts 50 to 2,000 sends, each mix within three standard errors of the generator's tally).
